===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*mey- (change)}}

From Late {{inh|en|enm|communite}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=commū̆nitẹ̄|pos=n|id=MED8643|accessdate=20 November 2017}}</ref> borrowed from {{der|en|fro|communité}}, {{m|fro|comunité}}, {{m|en|comunete}} (modern {{cog|fr|communauté}}), from Classical {{der|en|la|commūnitās||community; public spirit}},<ref>{{R:OED Online|entry=community|code=37337|part of speech=n}}</ref> from {{m|la|commūnis|commūn(is)|t=common, ordinary; of or for the community, public}} + {{m|la|-itās}}. {{surf|+suf|en|commune|ity|alt1=commun(e)}}. Displaced native {{noncog|ang|ġemǣnsċipe}}. {{doublet|en|communitas}}.

